    "Elliott JW. Response and outcome following metastasis occurring. •Cures may occur if tumor is found early and treated aggressively—median survival time for nonmetastatic tumors <3.2 cm in largest diameter was 1,237 days.",
    "McQuown B, Keyerleber MA, Rosen K, et al. •Growth of tumor may be slow and debulking lymph node metastatic disease burdens may significantly prolong survival. •Hypercalcemia variably associated with poor prognosis, with some studies showing it",
